      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then you can call the write function directly like this and pass it on to dbus:\n```\ntry {\n    stdplus::ManagedFd fd \u003d makeSealedCperFd(data);\n    auto ec \u003d ipmi::callDbusMethod(\n        ctx, Processor::default_service, Processor::instance_path,\n        Processor::interface, \"Process\",\n        sdbusplus::object_path(defaultInventoryPath), ContentType::CPERSection,\n        sdbusplus::message::unix_fd(fd.get()));\n    if (ec) { lg2::error(\"CPER Process failed: {MSG}\", \"MSG\", ec.message());\n\n              return ipmi::responseUnspecifiedError(); }\n}\ncatch (const std::exception\u0026 e)\n{ ... }\n```\n\nYou can see that it greatly reduces the complexity of the file handling and turns the pesky fd into an RAII situation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 343,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 363,
        "endChar": 5
      },
